@page
@model BeeMemoryBank.Web.Pages.Admin.RecoveryKeyModel

@section About {
    <p>
        A <strong>recovery key</strong> is a second way into the vault, for the day the administrator password is lost. It is issued by a superadmin, shown <strong>once</strong>, and
        kept <strong>offline</strong>: on paper or on a card in a safe place, not in the vault it protects. Only a key derived from it is stored on the node, never the key itself, so
        nobody, including this page, can show it to you again.
    </p>
    <p>
        With a recovery key, the Sign In page's <em>Forgot your password? Use a recovery key</em> sets a new password for a superadmin account (the <code>bmb</code> command line can
        do the same). It changes that one account's password and nothing else, and it does not open the vault by itself.
    </p>
    <p>
        Issuing a new key does not invalidate your passwords or your other recovery keys: make a new one if a copy was lost or seen by someone else, and keep the old ones until you are
        sure you no longer need them. <strong>A data-key rotation invalidates all recovery keys</strong>, so issue a new one right after it
        (<a href="/Admin/DekRotation">DEK Rotation</a>).
    </p>
}

<div class="card mt-md" style="max-width:640px;">
    <sl-button id="issue-recovery-key-btn" variant="primary" size="small">
        <sl-icon slot="prefix" name="key"></sl-icon>
        Issue new recovery key
    </sl-button>
    <div class="text-muted text-sm" style="margin-top:8px;">The key is shown in a window you have to close. Copy it before you do.</div>
</div>

<sl-dialog id="recovery-key-dialog" label="Your new recovery key" style="--width:560px;">
    <sl-alert variant="warning" open style="margin-bottom:12px;">
        <sl-icon slot="icon" name="exclamation-triangle"></sl-icon>
        Save this now. It is not stored anywhere in recoverable form and will never be shown again.
    </sl-alert>
    <sl-input id="recovery-key-value" readonly filled></sl-input>
    <sl-button slot="footer" id="recovery-key-copy" variant="primary">
        <sl-icon slot="prefix" name="clipboard"></sl-icon>
        Copy
    </sl-button>
    <sl-button slot="footer" id="recovery-key-close">Done</sl-button>
</sl-dialog>
